{"id":"ni43101:fde21413b31d5fe5","archive_url":"https://github.com/jaydeepdive/minemodelingpro/releases/download/report-archive/ni43101_fde21413b31d5fe5.pdf","report_url":"https://minedocs.com/21/Lagoa_Salgada_Project_TR-PEA_9212021.pdf","company":"Lagoa Salgada","project":"Lagoa Salgada","commodity":"Zn-Cu","jurisdiction":"Portugal","date":"2026-10-27","title_project":"Lagoa Salgada","cover_company":"Portugal Ascendant Resources Inc","extractor":"dt21","extracted":"2026-10-27T12:06:24Z","pages":305,"crs":{"zone":37,"hemi":"N","datum":"WGS84","zone_votes":{"37":2},"kind":"projected","epsg":32629,"crs_name":"WGS 84 / UTM zone 29N","source":"placed at report lat/long","dem_misfit_m":null,"z_units":null},"center":[38.22303,-8.44842],"text_center":[38.2333,-8.4667],"block_size":[10.0,10.0,10.0],"density":4.6,"sensitivity":null,"extent":{"strike":{"n":6,"min":500.0,"max":1700.0,"median":1700.0,"page":48,"text":"that all two deposits lie on a continuous coincidental IP chargeability anomaly with an estimated geological strike length of 1.7 km in an SSE to NNW direction from the South deposit to beyond"}},"attitude":{"dip_is_qualitative":true,"dip":{"n":4,"median":85.0,"min":70.0,"max":85.0,"page":35,"text":"erpreted to occur mostly on the subvertical-overturned and intensely faulted limb of a south-west-v"}},"geophysics":{"surveys":[{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":37,"text":"Recent Induced Polarization (IP) investigations conducted by Intelligent Exploration (IE) of Campbellford, Ontario, Canada, have successfully demonstrated that m"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":52,"text":"\u2022 Prepare an exploration programme. \u2022 Undertake ground and drillhole IP surveys. \u2022 Undertake diamond drilling (infill, step-out and metallurgical testwork drillholes). \u2022 Undertake detailed metallurgical testwork.","platform":"ground"},{"method":"magnetics","page":67,"text":"The consortium completed an airborne magnetic survey of the property and completed several widely spaced diamond drillholes.","platform":"airborne","year":1994},{"method":"borehole geophysics","page":67,"text":"In addition to the magnetic survey, RTZ performed limited downhole geophysics, electro-magnetic surveys, and limited soil sampling.","platform":"borehole","year":1994},{"method":"borehole geophysics","page":68,"text":"Portex\u2019s exploration activities included a drilling program and a downhole geophysical survey program. 6.2.4.1 DRILLING PROGRAM From May to August 2011, Portex completed five diamond drillholes on the LS deposit totallin","platform":"borehole"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":69,"text":"International Geophysical Technology (IGT) to conduct a downhole transient electromagnetic (TEM) geophysical survey in drillholes PX-02 and PX-05.","platform":"borehole"},{"method":"borehole geophysics","page":69,"text":"The drillhole steel collars were cemented in place and a steel cap was welded to the collars to allow for a hinged cap to co"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":80,"text":"Much of the earlier exploration work up to 2015 is described in Section 6. This section focuses on the more recent work.","year":2015},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":81,"text":"Historically both gravity and IP surveys have been used at LS. The exploration history of the property has been summarized in Section 6 of this Technical Report.","year":1994},{"method":"borehole geophysics","page":81,"text":"HOLE SURVEY In September and October 2017, IGT was contracted to complete a downhole geophysical survey in three drillholes: LS_MS_01, LS_MS_03 AND LS_MS_06.","platform":"borehole","year":2017},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":82,"text":"work led to a re-examination of historical Gravity data and the choice of Induced Polarization / Resistivity surveys (IP / Resistivity) to continue exploration in 2018 \u2013 2019.","year":2018},{"method":"magnetics","page":82,"text":"Magnetic surveys will not be able to detect this target. 9.3.2 GRAVITY AT LS The deposit was originally discovered during the drilling of a gravity anomal"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":83,"text":"83 Figure 9-1 - 2019 IP / Resistivity Survey Coverage Source: I.E. Intelligent Exploration 2019 There is a good agreement between the location of the known massive and stringe","year":2019},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":88,"text":"drill trajectories would have passed above the volume where the maximum chargeability occurs, deeper on the east side of the LS- South deposit.","year":2019,"platform":"borehole"}],"targets":[{"page":48,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"This interpretation is backed by geophysics which shows that all two deposits lie on a continuous coincidental IP chargeability anomaly with an estimated geological strike length of 1.7 km in an SSE to NNW direction from the South deposit to beyond the North d"},{"page":82,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"The Tertiary cover is much less dense (S.G. ~2.2). The basal conglomerate appears to be conductive over the known deposit, grading to higher resistivity away from the MS. Chargeability is associated with the Tertiary cover rocks, particularly over the deposit."},{"page":89,"explained":false,"untested":true,"text":"Agreement is good between the surface IP models and the BHIP, suggesting that both the North and South Resources are part of a single anomalous zone. The Central Zone remains largely untested by drilling, so the source of this anomaly remains to be identified."},{"page":91,"explained":false,"untested":true,"text":"Where these coincide with low resistivity and elevated gravity, they present good targets for follow-up drilling."},{"page":92,"explained":false,"untested":true,"text":"This recommendation from the 2018 program is carried forward and validated by the 2019 results. \u2022 Other surface IP / Res chargeability anomalies from the 2019 survey should be considered for follow-up drilling, especially when they are spatially correlated wit"},{"page":105,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"This interpretation is supported by geophysics which shows that all zones lie on a continuous coincidental IP chargeability anomaly with an estimated geological strike length of 1.7 km in an SSE to NNW direction from the South deposit to beyond the North depos"},{"page":296,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"This interpretation is backed by geophysics which shows that all two deposits lie on a continuous coincidental IP chargeability anomaly with an estimated geological strike length of 1.7 km in an SSE to NNW direction from the South deposit to beyond the North d"}]},"rock":null,"model_params":{"block":[10.0,10.0,10.0],"density":4.6,"composite_m":2.0,"radius_m":75.0,"method":"idw","power":3.0,"metallurgy":{"routes":["flotation"],"traits":["oxide","transitional","sulphide","arsenic"],"recoveries":{"Ag":65.0,"Au":66.0,"Cu":40.0,"Zn":25.0,"Pb":80.0},"summary":"oxide ore present, transitional ore present, sulphide ore, arsenic-bearing; processed by flotation to concentrate; stated recovery Pb 80%, Au 66%, Ag 65%, Cu 40%, Zn 25%"},"deposit_style":"pegmatite"},"effective_date":"2021-09-21","resource":{"page":38,"contained_unit":"t","categories":{"Measured":{"tonnes":47400,"grade":4.6,"contained":2127},"Indicated":{"tonnes":5457000,"grade":2.35,"contained":130000}},"year":null,"by_header":false,"cutoff":null,"cutoff_unit":null,"grade_unit":"%","scope":null,"element":null,"tonnes":5504400,"contained":132127,"mi_tonnes":5504400,"mi_contained":132127,"inf_tonnes":null,"inf_contained":null},"resource_rows":[{"page":38,"cat":"Indicated","cutoff":null,"cutoff_unit":null,"tonnes":1462000,"grade":0.08,"contained":2550000,"cunit":"lb","hist":false,"reserve":false,"pscore":3,"year":null,"total":false,"el":null,"grade_unit":"%","scope":null,"text":"Indicated GO 2.5 1,462 0.08 0.43 2.55 0.26 37 0.51 6.63 4.18 1.2 6.2 37.3 3.8 1,742.1 23.8"},{"page":38,"cat":"Measured","cutoff":null,"cutoff_unit":null,"tonnes":47400,"grade":4.6,"contained":2127,"cunit":"t","hi